        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Preserve Codex output after missing turn completion",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nSupersedes the patch from #99167 because the original contributor branch cannot be pushed to by `100yenadmin` despite `maintainerCanModify=true`.\n\n- Preserve captured assistant text only for no-side-effect Codex app-server `turn_completion_idle_timeout` failures from the completion-watch path.\n- Keep non-completion turn-watch timeouts, including progress-watch timeouts with assistant output, on the existing timeout/error path.\n- Add the missing regression test requested by ClawSweeper so assistant output from a non-completion timeout is not delivered as a successful reply.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nCodex app-server can do useful work and produce assistant output but then fail to emit the terminal `turn/completed` event. OpenClaw needs a narrow mitigation for the safe completion-timeout case so the user does not lose a final answer, while still failing closed for non-completion watchdogs and side-effectful turns.\n\nThe prior #99167 draft allowed assistant-output recovery whenever `shouldSurfaceCodexCompletionTimeout` was true. That predicate is broader than completion-watch timeouts, so a progress-watch timeout with assistant text could be delivered as a successful reply. This PR narrows delivery to `turnWatchTimeoutKind === \"completion\"`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRefs #87744 and #88312. Related historical items: #78756, #84076, #82080, #89974, and openai/codex#22144.\n\nFresh local evidence from `2026-07-03` shows the target failure class separately from the later subscription/usage-limit failure:\n\n- `2026-07-03 01:45 GMT+7`: `codex app-server turn idle timed out waiting for completion`, `failureKind=turn_completion_idle_timeout`, `turnWatchTimeoutKind=completion`, `lastActivityReason=turn:start`, `activeAppServerTurnRequests=0`, `activeTurnItemCount=0`, `terminalTurnNotificationQueued=false`.\n- `2026-07-03 02:24 GMT+7`: separate `rate_limit` / subscription usage-limit failure. This PR does not address that second failure.\n\nRed/green proof for the new regression:\n\n- RED on PR #99167 head before the code fix:\n  - `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-embedded-agent.config.ts --maxWorkers=1 --no-file-parallelism src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run.codex-app-server-recovery.test.ts`\n  - Failed: `does not deliver assistant output from non-completion Codex turn watch timeouts` received the assistant text as a successful payload.\n- GREEN after this patch:\n  - same command: `1 passed`, `12 passed`.\n- App-server event-stream proof:\n  - `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.turn-watches.test.ts -- --maxWorkers=1 --no-file-parallelism --reporter=dot`\n  - `1 passed`, `66 passed`.\n- Whitespace:\n  - `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n\nAfter-fix behavior proof on PR head `c53227734a6337507d4f538e049a7523e04e2ebf`:\n\nThe new head has the same tree as `b5d5a2abda40d10b14ec8213a9f0d1580c7148a8`; it was amended only to rerun upstream CI after an unrelated gateway-startup shard timeout.\n\n- Embedded runner delivery/fail-closed proof:\n  - `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-embedded-agent.config.ts --maxWorkers=1 --no-file-parallelism --reporter=verbose src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run.codex-app-server-recovery.test.ts`\n  - Passed scenarios include:\n    - `delivers safe assistant text after a missing turn/completed timeout`\n    - `does not deliver assistant output from non-completion Codex turn watch timeouts`\n    - `does not hand Codex app-server idle timeouts to model fallback`\n    - `does not retry after visible assistant output`\n  - Result: `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 12 passed (12)`.\n- Codex app-server turn-watch boundary proof:\n  - `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.turn-watches.test.ts -- --maxWorkers=1 --no-file-parallelism --reporter=verbose`\n  - Passed scenarios include:\n    - `marks Codex completion-idle timeouts after completed items as replay-invalid`\n    - `does not use completion timeout outcome for terminal timeout with active mutating item`\n    - `does not use completion timeout outcome for non-completion timeout with assistant output`\n    - `releases the session after a raw assistant response item without turn completion`\n    - `delivers completed assistant output when the client closes before turn completion`\n    - `keeps partial assistant output as a client-close failure`\n  - Result: `Test Files 1 passed (1)`, `Tests 66 passed (66)`.\n\n## Proof Boundary\n\nThis proves OpenClaw recovery/delivery behavior for the missing `turn/completed` completion-timeout mitigation. It does not claim the upstream Codex app-server root cause is fixed.\n",
